    "confidence": "high",
    "uncertainCells": [],
    "notes": "NON-MODERN PRINTING, named '-orig' to keep it apart from the modern-typeface 1961 card (batter_virdon-bill_1961). This is the classic-typeface 1961 Virdon card, shown twice in the 1600x970 scan (black ink in the middle, blue ink on the right; the left-hand card is the modern reissue). Unlike the one-sided original 1960, 1964 and 1965 cards, it is two-sided: its back in the post is a classic-format advanced side. The card carries no issue date, so it may be a later classic reissue rather than the first 1961-season issue. It differs from the modern printing in its grid arrangement only (same header ratings and statistics box): e.g. its WALKs sit at col3 r4-r5 rather than col1 r4/r12 and col2 r2/r3, and its HOMERUN 1 / flyball (rf) B split is at col1 r4 rather than col2 r9. Source: a 2019 collector's post of his Bill Virdon Strat-O-Matic cards (Wayback capture). Transcribed from 1.7x half-card crops of the black copy, then independently re-read from the blue copy, which agrees cell for cell. Col1 roll2 prints 'plus injury' under 'popout (2b)'; col2 roll2 'lineout (2b) into as many outs as possible' captured verbatim. 1961 BATTING RECORD box lists the seven stats AT BATS, DOUBLES, TRIPLES, HOMERUNS, AVERAGE, WALKS, STRIKEOUTS."
  }
